<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100">
  <.marketing_nav current_user={@current_user} current={:docs} />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <.docs_layout
      current="limits"
      updated="August 3, 2026"
    >
      <.docs_header current="limits">
        <:dek>
          The caps emisar enforces so one noisy action, one busy agent, or one aggressive export
          cannot overwhelm a page or the API. Most are generous. These are the ones worth knowing
          before you build against them.
        </:dek>
      </.docs_header>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Every cap says what you will actually observe when you reach it. The name links to the page
        that owns the behavior — the procedure lives there, not here.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-zinc-900">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-zinc-900 bg-zinc-950/80 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest text-zinc-500">
              <th class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium">What</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium">Cap</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium">At the cap</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-zinc-900 text-zinc-400">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/action-packs"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >Action output</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Set per action in the pack, separately for stdout and stderr — 64 bytes to 16 MiB
                across the shipped catalog
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Bytes past a stream's cap are dropped from the delivered output but counted, and
                stdout and stderr are each flagged truncated on their own.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link navigate={~p"/docs/runs"} class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200">Live output in the console</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">The most recent 500 progress lines</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Older lines are trimmed from the browser view with a note. Run history keeps
                accepted chunks within its durable budget. The host journal keeps bounded previews,
                byte counts, and hashes of the complete redacted streams.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/mcp-reference"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >MCP list pages</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                15 per page by default, with a maximum of 50.
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">recent_runs</code>
                supports up to 100.
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">find_actions</code>
                supports up to 15.
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Continue with the cursor the previous response returned. A catalog cursor is bound
                to its exact query and expires after 15 minutes.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/mcp-reference"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >MCP long-poll wait</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">Up to 60 seconds per call</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">run_action</code>
                and <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">wait_for_run</code>
                return the current state at the deadline. One credential can hold 8 concurrent waits
                per node. Every other tool answers immediately.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/mcp-reference"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >MCP structured output</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                8 KiB per run, shared down when one response carries several
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                A run whose parsed output is larger is dropped from the response and replaced with a
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">wait_for_run</code>
                continuation that fetches it on its own.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/mcp-reference"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >MCP response size</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">512 KiB per tool result</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Tools shrink themselves first — fewer rows, shorter output tails. A result that
                still does not fit returns a transport error carrying a
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">get_operation</code>
                continuation.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link navigate={~p"/docs/runbooks"} class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200">Runbooks</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                64 KiB definition. 32 inputs, 16 stages, 16 target refs per step, and 256 resolved
                items. A wait polls every 5 seconds to 1 hour for 2 to 100 attempts. A parallel
                stage runs 1 through 16 attempts at once, 5 unless the definition sets it. A title
                is at most 80 characters and 320 bytes, a description 4,096 characters and 8 KiB.
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Authoring or preflight rejects the definition before an execution is created. The
                MCP read budget is derived from these limits, so a saved runbook always fits one
                response.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link navigate={~p"/docs/runbooks"} class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200">Runbook execution</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                1 MiB frozen plan. 24 hours end to end, waits included
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Preflight rejects a plan that freezes larger. An execution still running at the
                deadline halts as timed out.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/audit-and-siem"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >Audit export</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">100 events per page, 1,000 maximum</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                A full page carries
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">Link: rel="next"</code>
                and there can be more right now. Keep paging from
                <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">X-Next-Cursor</code>
                while it does.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/audit-and-siem"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >Audit export requests</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">60 requests a minute per token</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                Further requests answer <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">429</code>. A poller must hold
                its cursor and retry rather than treat the failure as an empty page.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-zinc-200">
                <.link
                  navigate={~p"/docs/audit-and-siem" <> "#retention"}
                  class="text-brand-300 hover:text-brand-200"
                >Audit retention</.link>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                7 days on Free, 90 on Team, 365 on Enterprise
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6">
                The horizon is fixed per event when it is written, and terminal runs and their
                progress events follow the same window. Ingest into your SIEM to keep it longer.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <.docs_callout kind={:tip} title="Scripting against the API?">
        The fixed tools, identifiers, and recovery semantics of the emisar MCP server — including
        how a retried dispatch resolves to its original operation — are in the <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/mcp-reference"}
          class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300"
        >MCP CLI &amp; reference</.link>.
      </.docs_callout>
    </.docs_layout>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
